SECTION B: THM-4516 perfect-power clocks (independent census: residue sieve + exact roots, no gmpy2)
==============================================================================

B1. Dictionary. 2^K - q^X = +-m^r with q = p^s odd, K >= 1: m is odd (2^K - q^X is odd), p does not divide m
    (else p | 2^K), so gcd(m, 2p) = 1 and (2, p, m) with exponents (K, sX, r) is a primitive solution of
    x^a + y^b = z^c; Darmon-Granville finiteness applies when 1/K + 1/(sX) + 1/r < 1. By THM-4484(1) (clock | d)
    the shape (K,X) is free for T_{q, +-m^r} since the clock equals +-d. CONSISTENT (the converse is NOT claimed
    correctly in section 2.5 / THM-4516(5); see B5).

