C1. Proposition 3.2 re-derived.
    a_i = (4^i-1)/3: a_2..a_8 = [5, 21, 85, 341, 1365, 5461, 21845]; T(a_i) = 2^(2i-1): True
    a_i = 0 mod 3 iff 3 | i (i <= 200): True; ord_9(4) = 3
    a_i (i >= 2) is never a power of two (odd and > 1): True; the orbit after a_i is the trunk down to 1, so no orbit contains two distinct a_i: disjointness HOLDS
    odd preimage of n exists iff n = 2 mod 3 (n <= 10^5): True
    B(a) = {a} u B(2a) u B((2a-1)/3) (last term iff a = 2 mod 3), checked on n <= 2^18 for ten roots: True
    5 in B(16)? False (T(5) = 8 < 16). So 'B(4^i) = union_(i' >= i) B(a_i')' is off by one: B(2^(2i-1)) = trunk-above u union_(i' >= i) B(a_i'),
      and B(4^i) = trunk-above u union_(i' >= i+1) B(a_i'). Check: B(16) \ {16,32,64,...} == union_(i'>=3) B(a_i') on n <= 2^18: True; B(8) \ {8,16,32,...} == union_(i'>=2) B(a_i'): True
    B(5) u B(32) u {1,2,4,8,16} == B(1) on n <= 2^18 (this is the set reaching 1, i.e. all n only under Collatz): True; B(5) and B(32) disjoint: True
    Superadditivity of lower density on disjoint sets: liminf (A u B)/X >= liminf A/X + liminf B/X: standard. Proposition (iii) HOLDS.
    (iv) 'e_i sum to 1 iff almost every orbit reaches 1': the IF direction is proved (finite unions give lower density -> 1);
      the ONLY-IF direction needs dens B(2^(2M+1)) -> 0 as M -> oo (tightness of the entry index), which is not proved: OVERCLAIM.

C2. Sheet cap: a sheet-blind proof of 'every positive cycle basin has lower density >= c' transfers to 3x-1, whose three
    known positive cycles have disjoint basins, so 3c <= 1 and c <= liminf of each; if the densities exist, c <= min: HOLDS.
    The value quoted for the cap (0.3248) is the [1,2^29] count of the {5,7,10} basin; that basin is RISING (0.32505 on [2^31,2^32)),
    so the cap, if the limit exists, is >= 0.3250 (HYP-9165's own status text says so; its title still says 0.3248).

